      "content": "Pseudoscientific justifications often manifest as outdated or debunked biological determinism, where perceived in-group traits like \"cultural capacity\" or \"civilizational heritage\" are wrongly ascribed to immutable genetic characteristics. They frequently employ essentialist claims to differentiate groups, arguing that perceived differences in societal metrics—like intelligence or social cohesion—are inherent rather than environmental. This rhetoric frames out-groups as congenitally inferior or inherently disruptive, making the preservation of a biologically defined \"pure\" social structure appear akin to maintaining natural law. These claims are designed not as evidence, but as self-evident truths necessary to justify segregation and purity to their adherents.",
